At there moment there isn't really a lot of scope for combining the
things that you find in the dungeon to make other things.  This seems
like an obvious place where more depth could be added.

I'll kick off with these two:

1. It would be cool if chains had a use.  What if you could apply them
to a pet, and then apply them to a statue/staircase/fountain/other
fixed object and tether your pet?  This would mean that you could
leave dangerous pets in rooms to cover you from approching monsters,
keep them out of the way of shopkeepers/priests, and generally manage
them better.  This has been suggested before.

2. It would be so cool if you could #dip a mummy wrapping into a ! of
oil (and perhaps also booze?) to make a molotov cocktail.  This would
have an area effect when thrown (like the spell) but would be unstable
(like real molotov cocktails).  Perhaps any that were being carried
would explode if you fell down the stairs/into a pit or got hit by a
boulder?

